  "worked_solution": "Suppose $x$ is a real number. The greatest integer (or floor) function $\u230ax\u230b$ equals the greatest integer that is smaller than or equal to $x:$\n\n$$\n\u230ax\u230b=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n\\le x<n+1,\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of the greatest integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u230a-5\u230b=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
